dot/pull/107832#discussion_r2170297002","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107832","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2170297002"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107832#discussion_r2170297002"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107832"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2170297002/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":653,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":662,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":25,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2171660546","pull_request_review_id":2966070800,"id":2171660546,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6BcOkC","diff_hunk":"@@ -629,6 +629,9 @@ void JoltSoftBody3D::update_rendering_server(PhysicsServer3DRenderingServerHandl\n \tconst int physics_vertex_count = (int)physics_vertices.size();\n \n \tnormals.resize(physics_vertex_count);\n+\tfor (Vector3 &n : normals) {\n+\t\tn.zero();\n+\t}","path":"modules/jolt_physics/objects/jolt_soft_body_3d.cpp","commit_id":"dd80a3aa199b8f5d62bff7f9f889559ded68642f","original_commit_id":"8aa936d41ce5d44c35445a0a50bd9806b0250c60","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"If we're changing things anyway, then I would either change this to use `resize_uninitialized`, or just restore `normals.clear()` again. Either one is fine with me.\r\n\r\n```suggestion\r\n\tnormals.resize_uninitialized(physics_vertex_count);\r\n\tfor (Vector3 &n : normals) {\r\n\t\tn.zero();\r\n\t}\r\n```\r\n```suggestion\r\n\tnormals.clear();\r\n\tnormals.resize(physics_vertex_count);\r\n```\r\n\r\nLooks good otherwise.","created_at":"2025-06-27T11:13:00Z","updated_at":"2025-06-27T11:16:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107832#discussion_r2171660546","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107832","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2171660546"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107832#discussion_r2171660546"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107832"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2171660546/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":631,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":634,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":6,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2172979374","pull_request_review_id":2968186897,"id":2172979374,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6BhQiu","diff_hunk":"@@ -643,9 +646,15 @@ void JoltSoftBody3D::update_rendering_server(PhysicsServer3DRenderingServerHandl\n \n \t\tconst Vector3 normal = (v2 - v0).cross(v1 - v0).normalized();\n \n-\t\tnormals[i0] = normal;\n-\t\tnormals[i1] = normal;\n-\t\tnormals[i2] = normal;\n+\t\tnormals[i0] += normal;\n+\t\tnormals[i1] += normal;\n+\t\tnormals[i2] += normal;\n+\t}\n+\tfor (Vector3 &n : normals) {\n+\t\treal_t len = n.length();\n+\t\tif (len > CMP_EPSILON) {\n+\t\t\tn /= len;\n+\t\t}","path":"modules/jolt_physics/objects/jolt_soft_body_3d.cpp","commit_id":"dd80a3aa199b8f5d62bff7f9f889559ded68642f","original_commit_id":"8aa936d41ce5d44c35445a0a50bd9806b0250c60","user":{"login":"simpkins","id":163549,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzU0OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/163549?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins","html_url":"https://github.com/simpkins","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Sure, I'll add a comment.\r\n\r\nNote that this code is basically just copied from the Godot physics implementation here:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/ebc36a722593a131f0b1d88aa85f9e24d82b0766/modules/godot_physics_3d/godot_soft_body_3d.cpp#L185-L190\r\n\r\nI ultimately think that we should move this code out of the physics server implementation, and into SoftBody3D.  It doesn't seem like rendering shading logic belongs in the physics server, and it seems unfortunate that all physics server implementations have to re-implement this.  I have some discussions of this (and other issues) in this proposal:\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12670","created_at":"2025-06-27T23:38:26Z","updated_at":"2025-06-27T23:38:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107832#discussion_r2172979374","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107832","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2172979374"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107832#discussion_r2172979374"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107832"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2172979374/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":653,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":662,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2170297002,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":25,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2172983542","pull_request_review_id":2968192788,"id":2172983542,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6BhRj2","diff_hunk":"@@ -629,6 +629,9 @@ void JoltSoftBody3D::update_rendering_server(PhysicsServer3DRenderingServerHandl\n \tconst int physics_vertex_count = (int)physics_vertices.size();\n \n \tnormals.resize(physics_vertex_count);\n+\tfor (Vector3 &n : normals) {\n+\t\tn.zero();\n+\t}","path":"modules/jolt_physics/objects/jolt_soft_body_3d.cpp","commit_id":"dd80a3aa199b8f5d62bff7f9f889559ded68642f","original_commit_id":"8aa936d41ce5d44c35445a0a50bd9806b0250c60","user":{"login":"simpkins","id":163549,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzU0OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/163549?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins","html_url":"https://github.com/simpkins","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/simpkins/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'll update it back to using `clear()` again.\r\n\r\nI believe using `resize_uninitialized()` is not allowed here, and would technically be undefined behavior.  Even though `Vector3` is a standard-layout class, it has a non-trivial constructor, and I believe the standard says it's undefined behavior to access the data without running the constructor.\r\n(See section 11.9.5 of n4917.pdf: https://github.com/cplusplus/draft/releases/tag/n4917)","created_at":"2025-06-27T23:47:29Z","updated_at":"2025-06-27T23:47:29Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107832#discussion_r2172983542","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107832","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2172983542"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107832#discussion_r2172983542"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107832"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2172983542/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":631,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":634,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2171660546,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR"